Subject: [PATCH] Use an explicit four GiB memory budget on WebAssembly

The browser build uses wasm32 with MAXIMUM_MEMORY=4GB. Use 4096 MiB
as its configured RAM budget instead of repeatedly warning about the
unsupported native physical-memory query. This is a budgeting value,
not a measurement of the host's physical RAM or available memory.

diff --git a/libs/image/kis_image_config.cpp b/libs/image/kis_image_config.cpp
--- a/libs/image/kis_image_config.cpp
+++ b/libs/image/kis_image_config.cpp
@@ -428,7 +428,11 @@ int KisImageConfig::totalRAM()
     int totalMemory = 1000; // MiB
     int error = 1;
 
-#if defined Q_OS_LINUX
+#if defined __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // Explicit browser memory budget, matching MAXIMUM_MEMORY=4GB.
+    totalMemory = 4096;
+    error = 0;
+#elif defined Q_OS_LINUX
     struct sysinfo info;
 
     error = sysinfo(&info);
